Thanks for the nudge, good call! Pushed in dd635b78: `--argument` and `--option`, repeatable, with the `name[:type]` syntax of `--field`. The type defaults to `string` for an argument and `bool` for an option, a trailing `?` makes an argument optional (the way it makes a field nullable), and passing any of them skips the questions:

```
bin/console make:command app:send-report --argument=recipient --argument=cc:array? --option=dry-run --option=retries:int
```

While at it, I closed three holes the interactive mode had: an argument after an array one, a parameter named `io`, and an argument and an option sharing a name. Each now gets a clear error instead of a generated command that fails to load.

The 3 red "highest deps" jobs are unrelated: `TranslationBundle` not found in framework-bundle, same as last night's 1.x run.

